## Knight side swapping (knight-side-swap), generated from the Rosie teaching script (english-input.txt) under the world conventions.
##
## Instructor statements used (numbers as in english-input.txt):
##   4. If a clear location is jumpable by a block then you can move the block onto the clear location.
##   5. If a location is not below an object then it is clear.
##   6. If an object that is alongside a block is diagonal with a location that is not next to the block then the location is jumpable by the block.
##  11. The goal is that all the red blocks are on the red locations and all the blue blocks are on the blue locations.
## World: init-ksideswap2.world
##
## Translation (tools/rosie-language.md gives the general reading; the assumption ledger is in README.md):
##   - Operator move (argument1 = the block, argument2 = the clear location it moves onto), statement 4.
##   - jumpable (statement 6) is a static relation jumpable(L, F) between locations, computed from the world file's alongside,
##     diagonal-with and near relations with the block standing for the location F it is on (A-S1, A-S3): the knight's move.
##   - clear is a maintained one-argument relation (statement 5).
##   - The goal (statement 11) is expanded over the blocks of the world file (A-S2). "The solution has four steps" (statement 7)
##     is checked against the plans, not used.
## Matching hints for learned rules (World-Conventions L3-095, L11-009): many-valued attributes, sized from the initial world.
production optimize-attribute object 31
production optimize-attribute on 14
production optimize-attribute below 14
production optimize-attribute clear 16
production optimize-attribute jumpable 48


## Propose initialize-knight-side-swap when its conditions below hold.
sp {knight-side-swap*propose*initialize-knight-side-swap
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^world <w> -^name)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <o> + >)
   (<o> ^name initialize-knight-side-swap ^task-operator false)
}

sp {knight-side-swap*apply*initialize-knight-side-swap
